### what the two shots buy this verdict
M1 reddens exactly the tests that read the product over every scalar and compare against the ruling list, and M2 reddens
the named-Cf escape tests, on DIFFERENT lines. So the census tables WASHED/RAW column is not a reading of a comment: it is
pinned by in-repo nails that go red in both directions. The census claim '名单外不洗' therefore has teeth, and its 155-row
OUT set is what those nails would have contradicted had the boundary covered the whole Cf category.

